{"code":"122","title":"Digital Network Exploitation Analyst (DNEA)","category":"operations","categoryLabel":"Cyber operations","description":"Study digital networks and communications to support authorized intelligence and cyber operations.","updated":"2026-09-15","pending":true,"titles":[],"competencies":[],"qualifications":{},"militaryOccupations":[{"title":"1721 - Cyberspace Warfare Operator","service":"M"}],"roleDefinition":"The DNEA analyzes intercepted intelligence information for metadata and content. They use this data to reconstruct and document target networks to judge the intelligence value and maintain target continuity. DNEAs understand and analyze target implementation of communication technologies and digital network systems. They discover methods and suggest strategies to exploit specific target networks, computer systems, or specific hardware and/or software."}